hite_wool\",\n    \"barrel\",\n    \"flower_pot\",\n    \"oxeye_daisy\",\n    \"oak_leaves\",\n    \"oak_log\",\n    \"short_grass\",\n    \"spruce_fence\",\n    \"spruce_fence_gate\",\n    \"spruce_trapdoor\",\n    \"spruce_stairs\",\n    \"spruce_slab\",\n    \"composter\",\n    \"water_cauldron\",\n    \"farmland\",\n    \"water\",\n    \"carrots\",\n    \"potatoes\",\n    \"beetroots\",\n    \"wheat\",\n    \"pink_terracotta\",\n    \"brown_mushroom_block\",\n    \"red_terracotta\"\n  ],\n  \"changes\": [\n    \"Saved the unmodified generated image as concept.png in the current directory.\",\n    \"The role lists retain every planned block, including blocks not visible in the image. Visible material ids are interpretations of raster concept art, not a verified Minecraft block inventory; flower species, crop varieties and some timber or stone variants cannot be determined exactly.\",\n    \"The left elevation shows slight top-surface visibility at the pavement and projecting details, rather than a strictly orthographic projection.\",\n    \"Exact plot dimensions, house and wing footprints, nine-block shop opening and 33-block ridge height are not demonstrated by a measurable block grid.\",\n    \"Each home floor has three individual sash-style windows rather than three clearly paired window assemblies.\",\n    \"The loft window is much larger than a small loft opening and has added shutters.\",\n    \"White window mullions and thin frames use shapes that glass_pane and the specified quartz blocks cannot reproduce at the depicted scale.\",\n    \"Added flower boxes under all three lower home-floor windows, small shop plants, and lanterns visible inside the home windows. White flowers are approximated as oxeye_daisy in the palette.\",\n    \"The BUTCHER lettering is rendered as raised solid white characters rather than visibly constructed banner lettering.\",\n    \"The hanging sign adds a white meat-cleaver emblem and a thin metal bracket whose exact shape is not reproducible with the specified blocks.\",\n    \"Added hanging meat displays behind the counter. Their curved silhouettes, hooks and small cuts are not literal vanilla block geometry.\",\n    \"Counter goods are miniature pink, tan and red chunks rather than full block-sized terracotta and mushroom blocks; the brown goods appear considerably lighter than brown_mushroom_block.\",\n    \"The awning has thin fabric-like edges and sloping surfaces rather than fully block-thick wool construction.\",\n    \"The front door fanlight contains ornate thin latticework beyond ordinary glass_pane geometry, and the timber hood has a more elaborate stepped pediment.\",\n    \"Dormers are represented in both side slopes by the elevation, but only the east dormer is clearly visible in the three-quarter view.\",\n    \"The rear wing appears substantially exposed to the east in the three-quarter view; its required placement off the west half and exact two-storey height cannot be confirmed.\",\n    \"The east gravel passage opens through a broad wooden gate near the front of the garden, rather than clearly terminating at a rear garden gate. Its lamp post has a dark slender support rather than an unambiguous spruce_fence post.\",\n    \"Gravel is the dominant garden access surface; separate dirt_path routes from both the kitchen and shop back doors are not clearly shown.\",\n    \"Added a subdividing garden fence, substantial oak-leaf hedges, timber-edged beds and extra barrels.\",\n    \"The tree contains no identifiable apples. All four requested crop varieties are suggested, but potatoes cannot be distinguished reliably from the other green crops.\",\n    \"The back wing and main house obscure rear doors and part of the garden; a distinct shop back door is not visible.\",\n    \"The pavement resembles stone_bricks and stone_brick_slab in addition to the planned street palette, and dark chimney caps suggest deepslate_brick_slab.\",\n    \"Smoking chimney caps show exposed flames; the